// EXPECT: [E087]
// ★ A LIVE HOLE, half one. `addto(var x, x)` passes one array to two parameters of a call that
// WRITES one of them. Both lower to `int32_t* restrict`, so the emitted `addto(v0, v0)` hands one
// pointer to two `restrict` parameters — undefined behaviour by the C standard, whatever a given
// optimiser does with it.
//
// Accepted until 2026-09-26 because the borrow pass's loan classifier enumerated the aggregate
// kinds as `IRT_PTR || IRT_STRUCT || IRT_SLICE` and omitted `IRT_ARRAY`, so an array argument was
// not a loan and the co-argument check never compared two of them. `annot.h` — the code that emits
// the `restrict` — DOES count a decayed fixed array as a reference. Two lists had to agree about
// what a reference is and only one was maintained.
//
// The sibling shape `vadd(4, a, a[0..4])` (coarg_alias_subslice_fail.ln) was always caught, because
// there the two places share a base offset; this one needed the array kind to be a loan at all.
func addto(var out i32[4], a i32[4]) {
    var i usize = 0
    while i < 4 {
        out[i] = out[i] +% a[i]
        i = i + 1
    }
}
func main() i32 {
    var x i32[4] = [1, 2, 3, 4]
    addto(var x, x)
    return x[0]
}
